1
00:00:01,584 --> 00:00:07,090
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

2
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:10,719
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

3
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,887
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

4
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,349
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

5
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:17,934
Staff: The loan applicant

6
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:19,269
is here for the interview.

7
00:00:19,352 --> 00:00:21,938
Atoy: I import and sell
jewelries, bro.

8
00:00:22,021 --> 00:00:23,398
Do you have a sample?

9
00:00:23,481 --> 00:00:24,232
Sample?

10
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:28,778
Host: Your MVP, Rommel Romero!

11
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:29,738
[cheering]

12
00:00:29,821 --> 00:00:33,575
Audience: MVP! MVP!
[ball thudding]

13
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:34,743
MVP!

14
00:00:34,826 --> 00:00:35,869
Gavin: Rommel, Rommel!

15
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:38,204
They've been calling you
for a while.

16
00:00:38,288 --> 00:00:39,873
Where is he?

17
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:42,792
Belladonna: He needs to take
responsibility for our child!

18
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:44,210
Ronan!

19
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:46,087
Excuse me for a minute.

20
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:46,713
Atoy: Mmm.

21
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:48,840
You said you'd take responsibility
for me.

22
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:49,966
I'm sorry, miss.

23
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:51,801
But I really don't know you.

24
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:52,385
[device blips]

25
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:56,181
Atoy: I won’t get a loan from
this bank anymore.

26
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,433
How can I trust this bank,

27
00:00:58,516 --> 00:01:01,102
if the character of the manager
is questionable?

28
00:01:01,186 --> 00:01:02,812
I'd recognize her if she
were my mistress.

29
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:03,772
Gotcha!

30
00:01:03,855 --> 00:01:04,773
Gavin: You're always
smiling

31
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:06,733
whenever you’re typing
on your phone.

32
00:01:06,816 --> 00:01:07,484
Oh, who is that?

33
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:08,735
Rommel: Chanty.

34
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:10,236
Rommel: Chanty of…

35
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:11,488
ChantyPop Sweethearts.

36
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:13,239
Is she here already?

37
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:13,948
[phone blips]

38
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:16,451
Just stand by for whatever
mission

39
00:01:16,534 --> 00:01:17,619
is needed. Okay?

40
00:01:17,702 --> 00:01:19,245
- Copy, Master Cutter.
- Atoy: Thank you.

41
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:21,206
Where are you now?

42
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:22,624
I'm here at the shop.

43
00:01:22,707 --> 00:01:24,042
Is Atoy there?

44
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:25,043
No, he's not.

45
00:01:25,126 --> 00:01:26,795
Do you really feel
suspicious?

46
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:28,338
Have you really noticed
something?

47
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:30,673
Host: Our very own, Chanty!

48
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:33,218
[exclaiming & whooping]

49
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:34,511
Oh my gosh!

50
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:36,638
[lively chatter]

51
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:39,516
Ibyang: Why did we
think of…

52
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:40,892
having a picnic?

53
00:01:41,392 --> 00:01:43,269
Of course, I missed you.

54
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:45,939
Let's just join Mommy's
zombie run.

55
00:01:46,022 --> 00:01:46,523
They'll really do that!

56
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:48,024
And then eat the people!

57
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:49,776
[squealing, lively chatter]

58
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:51,277
[music fades]

59
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:54,155
Bro, ah. This is what you'll do
to the defender,

60
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:55,615
because I noticed, bro,
you can't get past

61
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:56,950
- the defender, right?
- That's true.

62
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:57,742
You have to stay low.

63
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:58,743
And then jump, you know.

64
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:00,286
And when you fake, of
course he'll jump.

65
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:00,870
Yes, yeah.

66
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:02,080
Attack the hip.

67
00:02:02,163 --> 00:02:03,164
Then you stay low.

68
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:04,332
Then make sure

69
00:02:04,415 --> 00:02:06,167
the ball has touched the ground
before you lift it,

70
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:07,377
because you're traveling,
bro, you know.

71
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:08,128
When you do it.

72
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:09,629
You lift it right
away, right?

73
00:02:09,712 --> 00:02:11,464
So fake, stay low.

74
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:13,758
Dribble, then
finish strong.

75
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:15,009
Okay, okay, okay,
okay.

76
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:16,594
- Okay? Do you get it?
- Got it, got it, got it. Yes.

77
00:02:16,678 --> 00:02:17,178
My turn.

78
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:19,055
Oh, game, okay.

79
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:21,141
[phone ringing]

80
00:02:21,766 --> 00:02:22,600
Oh, okay, okay.

81
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:24,269
[phone ringing]

82
00:02:25,186 --> 00:02:25,895
Gavin.

83
00:02:25,979 --> 00:02:26,896
Yes, Coach?

84
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,314
- Rommel: Oh, what a waste.
- Thank you.

85
00:02:28,398 --> 00:02:28,982
Coach?

86
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:31,776
That was hard.

87
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:32,569
[ball thuds]

88
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:36,197
[action music playing]

89
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:37,615
Rommel Romero.

90
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:40,994
How did you know my
surname?

91
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,413
Don't you remember me?

92
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:46,624
Well, no.

93
00:02:47,292 --> 00:02:49,794
Grade 3, Courage.

94
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:51,004
Sta. Elena School.

95
00:02:51,754 --> 00:02:53,214
Mrs. Castillo was our
adviser.

96
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,340
You bullied me back then.

97
00:02:55,258 --> 00:02:55,842
[music fades]

98
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:57,927
Huh, me? A bully?

99
00:02:58,011 --> 00:02:58,511
Maybe that wasn't me.

100
00:02:58,595 --> 00:02:59,596
Yes, it was you!

101
00:03:00,471 --> 00:03:02,056
I brought sundot-kulangot,

102
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,141
and then you told everyone

103
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:04,893
it really came from
my nose.

104
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:07,312
Our classmates stayed away
from me

105
00:03:07,395 --> 00:03:08,313
because of you!

106
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:11,566
Sorry.

107
00:03:11,649 --> 00:03:12,817
Oh, that was a long time ago.

108
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:16,613
And, I've changed.

109
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:17,780
You especially.

110
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:19,866
It looks like you're the one
who'd bully me.

111
00:03:19,949 --> 00:03:20,533
[titters]

112
00:03:21,159 --> 00:03:25,204
[sneaky music playing]

113
00:03:34,881 --> 00:03:36,007
What happened here?

114
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:38,551
Oh, nothing, bro.

115
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:43,723
Karla reminded me that we were
classmates in elementary.

116
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:45,808
Nice to meet you, Karla.

117
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:47,310
I hope we can be friends too.

118
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:49,437
[music continues]

119
00:03:50,146 --> 00:03:51,356
Ah, let's go.

120
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:52,190
Come on, let's play.

121
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:53,107
Coach called.

122
00:03:53,191 --> 00:03:53,858
What did he say?

123
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,151
Gavin: He said you still need
to practice.

124
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:56,277
[theme music playing]

125
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:57,237
Dude, play better.

126
00:03:57,779 --> 00:03:59,030
We're already practicing.

127
00:03:59,113 --> 00:04:01,908
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

128
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:05,662
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

129
00:04:07,288 --> 00:04:09,165
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

130
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:10,792
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

131
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:12,293
♪ The hole in my polo

132
00:04:12,377 --> 00:04:15,046
that's right under the armpit ♪

133
00:04:15,129 --> 00:04:16,881
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

134
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:18,633
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

135
00:04:18,716 --> 00:04:20,468
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

136
00:04:20,551 --> 00:04:25,056
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

137
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:26,224
[gunshots]

138
00:04:26,307 --> 00:04:27,809
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

139
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:29,852
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

140
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,437
[music swells]

141
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:35,650
[music fades]

142
00:04:37,318 --> 00:04:37,944
And I'll tell him.

143
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:38,987
Yes.

144
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:39,946
Oh?

145
00:04:40,029 --> 00:04:42,240
There, we're complete now.

146
00:04:42,323 --> 00:04:43,324
Listen up!

147
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:46,744
I called you, Tabang Lupa community,

148
00:04:46,828 --> 00:04:48,830
for this.

149
00:04:48,913 --> 00:04:49,956
Paldo: Zombie run.

150
00:04:50,039 --> 00:04:52,250
Velma: Zombie run, a fundraising
event.

151
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:54,877
Yes! Oh my, we still
need volunteers

152
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:57,213
to be zombies for the
runners.

153
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:58,506
So, sign up.

154
00:04:58,589 --> 00:05:00,049
Be a zombie?

155
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:02,051
Me, look like a monster?

156
00:05:02,135 --> 00:05:04,846
Oh, Jona, I'm not
vibing it.

157
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:07,223
Oh, sis, you know
me, look!

158
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:09,392
Being a zombie isn't
my branding,

159
00:05:09,475 --> 00:05:11,019
and running?

160
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:12,979
It's tiring, I don't
want to!

161
00:05:13,062 --> 00:05:14,188
Goodness, you have so
many complaints,

162
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:15,773
Tabang Lupa community!

163
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:18,651
This is healthy and will make you
beautiful, you need it.

164
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:20,236
Especially you, Velma!

165
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:21,529
Here, I'll do it.

166
00:05:21,612 --> 00:05:23,698
Oh, yes. Yes, babe.

167
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:25,575
Jona is right.

168
00:05:25,658 --> 00:05:26,951
And this is Audrey's project,

169
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:28,745
so let's support it.

170
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:29,370
Oscar: Mmm.

171
00:05:30,246 --> 00:05:32,123
Will you join, Oka?

172
00:05:32,206 --> 00:05:33,082
Mmm-mmm.

173
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:35,418
Well, it's Audrey's project, after all.

174
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:37,336
Then let's join.

175
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:38,713
- It looks fun, right?
- Yes.

176
00:05:38,796 --> 00:05:39,964
Yes, yes.

177
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:41,049
Sir Oka, like this?

178
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:42,759
[growling]

179
00:05:42,842 --> 00:05:43,384
Oh.

180
00:05:43,468 --> 00:05:45,678
Oh, wow! Wow!

181
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:46,971
When I invite you, you have
so many obje--

182
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:48,514
nyak, nyak, nyak, nyak!

183
00:05:48,598 --> 00:05:51,434
But when it's Papa Handsome,
you're totally game.

184
00:05:51,517 --> 00:05:53,686
I’m your neighbor here,
right?!

185
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:56,773
[growling]

186
00:05:56,856 --> 00:05:57,607
[chuckles & applauds]

187
00:05:57,690 --> 00:05:59,275
Siony: Yes! Yes, okay.

188
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:03,321
[growling]

189
00:06:03,404 --> 00:06:04,197
Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait.

190
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,448
I can't, we can't.

191
00:06:05,531 --> 00:06:06,407
Huh? Oh.

192
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:08,367
Why, Emerson?
This is fun.

193
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:10,286
No, you. Yes, you.

194
00:06:10,369 --> 00:06:11,579
And you, and me.

195
00:06:11,662 --> 00:06:13,873
We can't on that day,
we're busy!

196
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:14,457
Jona: Why--

197
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:16,000
we're looking for
proof of what

198
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:18,920
Miss Siony's cousin
complained about!

199
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:20,046
That jerk Elvis

200
00:06:20,129 --> 00:06:22,006
and his hussy Rochelle!

201
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:23,341
So, we can't join that run.

202
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:24,383
You, you join.

203
00:06:25,009 --> 00:06:26,219
[indistinct chattering]

204
00:06:26,302 --> 00:06:27,386
Let them be.

205
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:28,971
This is fun, healthy. Nice.

206
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:30,264
Well, but…

207
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:33,184
- Right? Zombie, zombie!
- Oh, let's join!

208
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:34,227
[growling]

209
00:06:37,688 --> 00:06:39,232
What is happening here?
[electricity buzzing]

210
00:06:39,315 --> 00:06:40,817
This is a new side effect.

211
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:42,693
Well, fix it.

212
00:06:42,777 --> 00:06:43,820
[electricity buzzing]

213
00:06:43,903 --> 00:06:45,279
We don't know how.

214
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:48,241
These do not belong to the
expected responses.

215
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:51,410
Laboratory head: Perhaps we should
pause with the trials first.

216
00:06:52,453 --> 00:06:56,165
Perhaps you should continue
with brainwash, huh.

217
00:06:56,249 --> 00:06:58,376
[electricity buzzing]

218
00:06:58,459 --> 00:07:02,088
[tense music playing]

219
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:12,473
[indistinct chattering]

220
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:13,433
Ibyang: We're here.

221
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:15,184
I need to pee.

222
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:17,186
Oh, get out now.

223
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,271
I'll carry your bags.

224
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:19,647
Yay.

225
00:07:19,730 --> 00:07:20,606
Ibyang: Thank you, Tatoy!

226
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:21,566
Of course!

227
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:23,443
- Whoa. Yay!
- Oh, go, go, go!

228
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:24,819
Okay. I need to pee!

229
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:26,154
- Yeah!
- Come on, come on!

230
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:28,364
[car door closes]

231
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:34,704
[soft drama music playing]

232
00:07:34,787 --> 00:07:36,122
You're not sulking anymore?

233
00:07:37,206 --> 00:07:40,084
[music continues]

234
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:42,837
How?

235
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:44,422
The kids are so happy.

236
00:07:45,923 --> 00:07:46,674
What about you?

237
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:50,386
Of course I'm
happy too.

238
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:54,974
Because finally, you're
with us.

239
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:58,144
The only reason I was
sulking is because…

240
00:07:59,103 --> 00:08:01,522
I miss this kind
of bonding.

241
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:04,442
I missed you.

242
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:07,320
We missed you.

243
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:09,572
I'm here now.

244
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:13,701
But of course, I
can't promise

245
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:14,911
that I won't…

246
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:16,579
be busy.

247
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:21,167
But I would always find
time for us.

248
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:25,213
[sentimental music playing]

249
00:08:35,139 --> 00:08:36,641
[music fades]

250
00:08:37,642 --> 00:08:39,143
- Brother, oh--
- Mmm?

251
00:08:39,227 --> 00:08:40,937
Apparently, there's chicken
and pizza?

252
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:42,063
- Chicken?
- Where is it?

253
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:45,149
Th--there, at
the back.

254
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:45,942
Oh, where, where,
where?

255
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:46,651
Oh, eat now.

256
00:08:46,734 --> 00:08:47,985
- Ah, at the back.
- Audrey: Here, look.

257
00:08:48,819 --> 00:08:50,446
- Get it, Gavin.
- We're rich today, ah!

258
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:52,281
Super, winner!

259
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:53,908
- Okay, go on in there.
- Karla: Thank you!

260
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:55,618
Let's go.

261
00:08:55,701 --> 00:08:57,161
- Okay.
- Oh, go ahead. I'll follow.

262
00:08:57,245 --> 00:08:58,037
Audrey: You go first, love.

263
00:08:58,788 --> 00:08:59,413
See you!

264
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:01,499
[car door closes]
Inside!

265
00:09:01,582 --> 00:09:02,291
All right.

266
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:05,294
[light music playing]

267
00:09:08,839 --> 00:09:12,051
[tense music playing]

268
00:09:39,203 --> 00:09:40,329
[crickets chirping in the distance]

269
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:43,541
I didn't see anything in the messages,
it's really clean.

270
00:09:44,125 --> 00:09:47,044
There's something in the
calendar, it says…

271
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:51,549
"Deliver 10 boxes of bacon
for F. Cohen.

272
00:09:51,632 --> 00:09:53,175
Pull out, 5 PM."

273
00:09:53,884 --> 00:09:55,261
Who is F. Cohen?

274
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:56,220
Frank Cohen.

275
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:58,806
That's Samir's alias.

276
00:09:59,348 --> 00:10:01,392
So, where are they meeting?

277
00:10:01,475 --> 00:10:02,226
[sighs]

278
00:10:02,727 --> 00:10:03,853
But you're right.

279
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:06,105
I don't believe they're
delivering bacon.

280
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:08,316
They're delivering money.

281
00:10:08,399 --> 00:10:09,650
[suspicious music playing]

282
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:11,402
Because if we can
trail that,

283
00:10:11,485 --> 00:10:13,654
maybe they'll lead us to the
Obsidian HQ.

284
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:15,948
Have you ever been to Obsidian?

285
00:10:16,949 --> 00:10:18,326
All independent contractors,

286
00:10:18,409 --> 00:10:19,619
the work is done outside.

287
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:22,330
That's why we need to
follow him now.

288
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:24,290
When, Sir?

289
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,250
Here's the thing, wait.

290
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:29,629
Shoot.

291
00:10:32,506 --> 00:10:34,383
It's at the same time as
Audrey's zombie run.

292
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:36,969
I can't not go there,

293
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:38,554
I promised her.

294
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:41,015
I've already let my family down
so many times.

295
00:10:41,098 --> 00:10:42,266
How about this, Sir.

296
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:45,186
I'll just tell Uno
and Jesabel

297
00:10:45,269 --> 00:10:46,395
about this mission.

298
00:10:46,937 --> 00:10:48,564
Just go be with your family.

299
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:50,650
Okay.

300
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:53,194
But, Belladonna,

301
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:55,780
you can't be seen by these
people. Okay?

302
00:10:55,863 --> 00:10:57,948
Tell Uno and Jesabel,

303
00:10:58,032 --> 00:10:58,824
they're in charge.

304
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:00,284
But please, you
cannot be seen.

305
00:11:01,035 --> 00:11:03,913
[pensive music playing]

306
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:08,167
Does that look like mine?

307
00:11:09,543 --> 00:11:10,670
It's not mine either,

308
00:11:10,753 --> 00:11:11,837
but I kind of like it.

309
00:11:12,963 --> 00:11:15,466
It would be even more awkward if I
wore that, wouldn't it?

310
00:11:16,008 --> 00:11:17,134
It's not mine.

311
00:11:17,218 --> 00:11:19,095
Why, Audrey? Why are
you asking

312
00:11:19,178 --> 00:11:20,096
whose it is?

313
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:22,765
Nothing.
It's, nothing.

314
00:11:22,848 --> 00:11:25,601
I saw this outside,
so I thought…

315
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:28,020
maybe it belongs
to one of you.

316
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:30,731
Because I'm sure this doesn't
belong to the kids.

317
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:33,025
Ah, sometimes someone goes
jogging outside.

318
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:34,318
Maybe it just fell.

319
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:36,570
Maybe so.

320
00:11:36,654 --> 00:11:39,407
[mysterious music playing]

321
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:41,450
What if we go jogging ourselves,
Karla?

322
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:43,285
GAVIN: Let's go
jogging.

323
00:11:44,078 --> 00:11:45,287
Okay, let's go.

324
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:47,790
Jogging? Just one
hour, okay?

325
00:11:48,332 --> 00:11:49,500
One hour.

326
00:11:49,583 --> 00:11:51,419
One hour is fine.

327
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:53,421
CITA: Just one hour.

328
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:03,639
[music swells]

329
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:05,224
[music fades]

330
00:12:05,891 --> 00:12:09,186
SIONY: And the man still
wouldn't admit it!

331
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:11,188
He kept trying to get away
with it!

332
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:13,816
That's why you really need
concrete evidence

333
00:12:13,899 --> 00:12:16,402
or you have to catch them in
the act yourself.

334
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:18,404
[heavy music playing]

335
00:12:22,658 --> 00:12:24,702
AUDREY: If I find out you
have another woman,

336
00:12:24,785 --> 00:12:27,371
I’ll kill you, Anthony Padua.

337
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:30,833
[music swells]

338
00:12:42,678 --> 00:12:43,596
ATOY: Yeah, Love?

339
00:12:43,679 --> 00:12:44,722
There are still plenty of
seats there, huh.

340
00:12:45,264 --> 00:12:46,390
- AUDREY: Okay.
- ATOY: Where should I put this?

341
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:47,808
Ah, just there.

342
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:49,101
- ATOY: Okay. Oh?
- Oh, Love, come here, come here!

343
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:50,978
- Are you okay there?
- I'll introduce you to my boss.

344
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:52,521
- ATOY: Boss?
- Oh, Ms. Dolly!

345
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:53,856
You're preparing so early.

346
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:54,815
- Hello!
- Good job.

347
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:55,774
Thank you so much!

348
00:12:56,192 --> 00:12:56,734
I'm glad you're happy.

349
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:59,278
Uhm, oh, by the way, this is
my husband, Atoy.

350
00:12:59,361 --> 00:13:01,197
Uhm, love, my new boss,
Ms. Dolly.

351
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,364
Hi, Ma'am.

352
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:03,157
Pleased to meet you.

353
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,408
Pleased to meet
you, Ma'am.

354
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:07,786
Hmm. Your husband is
quite handsome.

355
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:08,871
Oh, of course!

356
00:13:08,954 --> 00:13:09,538
[chuckles]

357
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:10,581
Hope he's a good boy, huh?

358
00:13:10,664 --> 00:13:11,790
Oh, yes, Ma'am.

359
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,584
Well, I'm loyal to my Love.

360
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:16,795
And very good answer.

361
00:13:18,005 --> 00:13:19,381
[phone ringing]

362
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:20,299
Ah, excuse me.

363
00:13:21,091 --> 00:13:22,676
[mellow music playing]

364
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:24,553
'Son?

365
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:26,096
Hello, 'Toy!

366
00:13:26,972 --> 00:13:28,474
Can I still catch up to…

367
00:13:28,557 --> 00:13:29,975
Audrey's zombie run?

368
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:31,018
I think, I think it's
still possible.

369
00:13:31,101 --> 00:13:32,186
It hasn't started yet.

370
00:13:32,269 --> 00:13:34,104
Okay, okay. I'll catch up.

371
00:13:34,605 --> 00:13:35,814
Because, uh…

372
00:13:35,898 --> 00:13:38,275
let me just finish this client’s
request here at the…

373
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:39,652
Children of the Thread office.

374
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:42,196
It's this Miss Tess…

375
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:43,989
[grunts]

376
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:46,116
Her smug husband, Elvis?

377
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,702
Yeah. Well, he thought…

378
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:53,207
uh, his wife wouldn't find
out that…

379
00:13:55,251 --> 00:13:56,919
he only wanted to join
that zombie run,

380
00:13:57,461 --> 00:14:01,006
to go on a date with
his side chick, Rochelle.

381
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:04,385
So, uh, let me just
take care of this first.

382
00:14:05,052 --> 00:14:06,011
Amazing.

383
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:07,680
It's like a TV drama, huh.

384
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:08,430
[smirks]

385
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,224
Yeah, right?
I know, right?

386
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:11,934
Okay, but I'll catch
up there, okay.

387
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:14,019
Oh, I'm just stretching.

388
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:16,730
Because it's the off-season
for marathons right now.

389
00:14:16,814 --> 00:14:18,482
Oh, okay, okay, okay. W
e'll wait for you.

390
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:20,484
Mmm, that's fine.

391
00:14:20,568 --> 00:14:21,735
Huh? But--

392
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:23,070
JESABEL: Hey, make sure to
wear a mask, okay.

393
00:14:23,612 --> 00:14:24,280
Yeah, that's fine too.

394
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:25,406
Where? Where?

395
00:14:26,574 --> 00:14:27,366
Wait for me!

396
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:31,620
Oh. Wai--wait a second.

397
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:33,873
Why are you dressed up?

398
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:35,416
You're not coming with us.

399
00:14:35,499 --> 00:14:36,458
I just have a gut feeling

400
00:14:36,542 --> 00:14:38,294
that you're gonna be needing backup.

401
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:40,087
You're not feeling well, right?

402
00:14:42,339 --> 00:14:43,340
Beatriz…

403
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:45,175
[sneaky music playing]

404
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:46,343
I think it would be better

405
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:48,262
if you just stay here.

406
00:14:48,345 --> 00:14:50,890
I'll wear a mask so no one
will recognize me.

407
00:14:51,932 --> 00:14:54,560
Oh, excuse me. No.

408
00:14:54,643 --> 00:14:56,478
As far as Sir Atoy knows,

409
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:58,647
only Uno and I are
leaving.

410
00:14:58,731 --> 00:14:59,440
Because our job

411
00:14:59,523 --> 00:15:00,691
is pretty easy anyway.

412
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:01,859
We're just going there,

413
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:03,193
we'll follow the van.

414
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:04,278
Right, Uno?

415
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:06,363
We can never tell.

416
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:07,656
Besides, I can fight.

417
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:09,283
So, I can be a big help.

418
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:10,284
Right, Uno?

419
00:15:10,367 --> 00:15:11,160
[music fades]

420
00:15:11,243 --> 00:15:11,869
JESABEL: What?

421
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:15,873
Oh, suit yourself.

422
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:18,125
[soft rock music playing]

423
00:15:18,208 --> 00:15:19,251
you need to wear this, right?
You probably know…

424
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:20,836
Ms. Dolly.

425
00:15:21,545 --> 00:15:22,838
Oh, invite the others there too.

426
00:15:24,131 --> 00:15:25,925
Of course, we'll support Audrey,

427
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:27,009
there at the Harvest--

428
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:29,720
Love, uh, who are you
talking to?

429
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:31,972
Emerson.

430
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:32,640
Ah.

431
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:34,308
Really?

432
00:15:35,392 --> 00:15:36,393
Ah, oh--yes.

433
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:37,353
So--'Son, oh.

434
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:39,563
Hi, Emerson!

435
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:41,315
Emerson on the phone: Hello, Audrey.

436
00:15:41,398 --> 00:15:42,024
[chuckles softly]

437
00:15:42,566 --> 00:15:43,067
Emerson on the phone: I'm joining,

438
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:44,568
and so are Paldo and
the others,

439
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:45,778
in the zombie run,
okay?

440
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:47,571
Emerson on the phone: I hope that's
still possible,

441
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:48,781
even though we weren't
able to register.

442
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,033
Ah, yes. That's still p
ossible.

443
00:15:51,116 --> 00:15:53,535
Uhm, thank you for the
support, okay.

444
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:54,370
See you later.

445
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:55,079
ATOY: Just in time?

446
00:15:56,872 --> 00:15:59,625
[pensive music playing]

447
00:15:59,708 --> 00:16:00,793
ATOY: Do you still need chairs?

448
00:16:01,335 --> 00:16:01,877
[phone blips]

449
00:16:01,961 --> 00:16:02,795
ATOY: I'll get some from there.

450
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:04,380
[suspicious music playing]

451
00:16:04,463 --> 00:16:05,297
BELLADONNA: I'm going out.

452
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:06,256
Don't worry.

453
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:09,885
I'll be careful so that no one will
see or recognize me.

454
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:11,971
[music continues]

455
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:15,182
Who is this Belladonna?

456
00:16:16,558 --> 00:16:20,229
[music swells]

457
00:16:35,786 --> 00:16:38,706
[pensive music playing]

458
00:16:39,415 --> 00:16:41,333
[camera shutter snapping]

459
00:16:41,417 --> 00:16:44,253
[music continues]

460
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,046
[phone blips]

461
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:47,297
[music continues]

462
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:48,215
[phone blips]

463
00:16:49,008 --> 00:16:51,552
[suspicious music playing]

464
00:17:00,269 --> 00:17:01,895
[music fades]

465
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:41,351
Hey. Go forward now, let's go.

466
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:43,687
Gavin, maybe we shouldn't join yet.

467
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:45,647
Let's just hang out somewhere else.

468
00:17:46,356 --> 00:17:46,857
Huh?

469
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:49,860
I can't. I promised I'd
support Aunt Audrey.

470
00:17:50,444 --> 00:17:51,070
Let's go!

471
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:52,446
Ah, no, no, no.

472
00:17:52,529 --> 00:17:53,280
We'll just be zombies instead.

473
00:17:53,363 --> 00:17:53,947
- Let’s go. Let’s go.
- Huh?

474
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:54,656
Let's go, let's go.

475
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:57,326
[suspicious music playing]

476
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:07,252
I'll fill one out too.

477
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:07,878
[music fades]

478
00:18:07,961 --> 00:18:08,712
Zombie?

479
00:18:08,796 --> 00:18:10,422
[indistinct chattering]

480
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:11,673
Oscar: There! Wow!

481
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:12,925
Oh. Hey, Oka!

482
00:18:13,008 --> 00:18:14,510
- Siony: Hey, Oka!
- Hey, guys, thank you!

483
00:18:14,593 --> 00:18:17,179
Thank you for agreeing to
volunteer as zombies.

484
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:18,388
Wow.

485
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:20,724
Oh, thank you! Do your
best later, okay!

486
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:21,850
Oh, zombie pose!

487
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:23,852
[SCREAMING & GROWLING]

488
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:26,688
[EXCLAIMING & LAUGHING]

489
00:18:26,772 --> 00:18:28,023
This is too much.

490
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:28,607
Oh, sorry.

491
00:18:28,690 --> 00:18:29,525
Sorry, we're the zombies.

492
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:30,359
Let me check outside again.

493
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:31,568
Oh, okay, okay,
Sir Oka.

494
00:18:31,652 --> 00:18:32,611
I'll be back; I'll be back.

495
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:33,737
Thank you!

496
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:37,449
Aww, joining the run
looks so fun!

497
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:38,492
It’s unfair.

498
00:18:38,575 --> 00:18:41,161
Hey, Ame! You can't join!

499
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:43,330
You might just get stepped
on there!

500
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:45,874
Ah, I just don't want her
getting hurt.

501
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:46,875
You’re exaggerating.

502
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:48,710
Just because I'm the only
small one here.

503
00:18:48,794 --> 00:18:49,461
Miss Siony, gosh.

504
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:50,671
Paldo: Oh, no. Not at all.

505
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:52,756
Well, Miss Siony is just
worried about you.

506
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:54,174
Of course, because--

507
00:18:54,716 --> 00:18:56,301
Don't be upset now.

508
00:18:56,844 --> 00:19:02,057
[TEASING, EXCLAIMING, GIGGLING]

509
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:06,854
That guy is so annoying…

510
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:08,272
that Oka.

511
00:19:08,856 --> 00:19:11,024
His face irritates me.

512
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:13,360
Just wait, I'll keep an
eye on him later.

513
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:15,195
He's gonna get it
from us, right?

514
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:18,157
I thought the traitor Elvis

515
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:20,784
and that snake Rochelle were the
reason we came here.

516
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:23,954
Well, they are.
That's really it.

517
00:19:24,037 --> 00:19:26,165
But we can do a side
quest too.

518
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:27,207
With that Oka guy.

519
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:29,001
He's really pissed
at Oka, huh?

520
00:19:29,668 --> 00:19:31,086
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

521
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:32,963
Oka the Annoying!

522
00:19:33,046 --> 00:19:35,048
Oh, zombies, are you ready?!

523
00:19:35,132 --> 00:19:36,175
Let's go!

524
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:37,926
[GROWLING]

525
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:42,472
[pleasant music playing]

526
00:19:54,484 --> 00:19:57,696
[PHONE RINGING]
[GROWLING]

527
00:20:01,241 --> 00:20:03,577
Hello? Where are you now?

528
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:08,248
[MUFFLED CHATTERING]

529
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:11,210
Belladonna: Positive, Sir.

530
00:20:11,293 --> 00:20:13,003
They're loading something
into the van.

531
00:20:13,086 --> 00:20:15,172
Looks like these are the
boxes of "bacon",

532
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:17,132
a.k.a. Obsidian money.

533
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:18,884
Ju--ju--just keep an eye
on it, okay?

534
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:20,219
And, uh, keep me posted.

535
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:22,930
Belladonna: We'll take care
of it, Master Cutter.

536
00:20:24,264 --> 00:20:27,267
[suspicious music playing]

537
00:20:27,351 --> 00:20:27,935
Okay.

538
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:30,812
[music fades]

539
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:32,648
Hey, Audrey.

540
00:20:33,732 --> 00:20:34,608
What's that? Are you
changing clothes?

541
00:20:34,691 --> 00:20:36,235
Your running outfit
is fine.

542
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:38,195
And those are for
the zombies.

543
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:40,530
[pensive music playing]

544
00:20:40,614 --> 00:20:42,241
I'm going to be
a zombie.

545
00:20:42,324 --> 00:20:43,909
Hmm? Why?

546
00:20:45,953 --> 00:20:49,248
A Belladonna texted Atoy.

547
00:20:50,749 --> 00:20:51,959
Be--Belladonna?

548
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:53,377
[music intensifies]

549
00:20:53,961 --> 00:20:55,587
What--what--what
did she say?

550
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:56,672
[music continues]

551
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:57,381
[sighs]

552
00:20:57,464 --> 00:20:58,715
How would I know
who she is.

553
00:20:59,424 --> 00:21:01,510
All she said was that
she's coming.

554
00:21:03,762 --> 00:21:06,431
Oka, I really have
a feeling that…

555
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:07,933
something is going
on between

556
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:08,976
her and Atoy.

557
00:21:11,478 --> 00:21:13,438
That's why I'm keeping an
eye on my husband.

558
00:21:15,232 --> 00:21:17,359
[tense music playing]

559
00:21:24,116 --> 00:21:25,033
[pleasant music playing]

560
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:27,869
Love, where are you?

561
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,414
Audrey on the phone:
Ah, I'm joining the run!

562
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:32,624
I'm in costume too, love.

563
00:21:33,458 --> 00:21:35,711
Love, hello?

564
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:38,839
Hey, it’s beautiful!

565
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:40,382
Hey.

566
00:21:40,465 --> 00:21:41,049
Love!

567
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:43,677
Love, I'm here!

568
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:46,263
Audrey: I'm your zombie
bride!

569
00:21:47,472 --> 00:21:48,265
[GROWLS]

570
00:21:48,348 --> 00:21:51,351
Till death do
us part!

571
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:52,728
[GROWLS]

572
00:21:52,811 --> 00:21:54,646
[music continues]

573
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:55,397
Okay.

574
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:56,606
[music swells]

575
00:21:56,690 --> 00:22:01,611
[ELECTRONIC BLIPPING]

576
00:22:01,695 --> 00:22:06,742
[intense music playing]

577
00:22:06,825 --> 00:22:08,618
What are we even going to do
at that zombie run?

578
00:22:08,702 --> 00:22:10,245
We're wasting our time.

579
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:14,124
Elias: Instead of building a
case against that Atoy!

580
00:22:14,207 --> 00:22:15,167
[theme music playing]

581
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:16,001
[lively chatter]

582
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:17,419
Brother, are you okay?

583
00:22:17,502 --> 00:22:18,378
Hey--aargh!

584
00:22:19,087 --> 00:22:19,629
Hey. Oh, my, oh, no!

585
00:22:19,713 --> 00:22:20,714
[LAUGHS]

586
00:22:20,797 --> 00:22:22,007
Hello, Master Cutter.

587
00:22:22,090 --> 00:22:24,926
Be advised. Target vehicle
is on the move.

588
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:26,178
Get down from there!

589
00:22:26,261 --> 00:22:27,471
[music continues]

590
00:22:27,554 --> 00:22:29,681
[GRUNTING & GROANING]

591
00:22:29,765 --> 00:22:31,808
[THUMPING & THUDDING]

592
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:32,976
[music swells]

593
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:33,643
I told you, you shouldn't--

594
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:34,770
don't call.

595
00:22:34,853 --> 00:22:35,896
SOS.

596
00:22:35,979 --> 00:22:36,646
Belladonna: We're cornered.

597
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:38,231
We're here on
Delgado Street.

598
00:22:38,315 --> 00:22:38,899
On my way.

599
00:22:38,982 --> 00:22:39,691
I'm on my way.

600
00:22:39,775 --> 00:22:42,861
["Mamang Sastre" PLAYING]
